y in production. After the rollback, all regions report v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Next step: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 15029, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01CTvnbVBKV623F8xsvLikdu", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 15029, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01CTvnbVBKV623F8xsvLikdu", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 19303, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident.\n\n- **Problem:** v2.3.1 was live in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an 18% error rate. The test build before it (v2.3.1-rc) had also failed health checks in staging.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production, so I rolled back to it. All three regions now run v2.3.0 and pass health checks, with the error rate down to 0.2%. Change-manager approval wasn't needed because v2.3.0 has been healthy in production before.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) is open and has paged the on-call engineer. It covers the failure, the rollback, the current status, and a note to find out why v2.3.1 failed before deploying it again.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01EQT6qSfXopxMwNPDNXP5ru", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01N1PrUUcA6z6onT5S38AtiM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01UV64WMmkPJheBrQFYjRhGk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Wtqb5eERChQSMPsRJZ8LH9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01AqvjXAqySCurKXq3sArip5", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01CTvnbVBKV623F8xsvLikdu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the deploy of checkout-api v2.3.1 to production (us-east, us-west, eu-west), the service failed health checks with an error rate of 18%. The release candidate v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. checkout-api was rolled back in all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all regions report v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Next step: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident.\n\n- **Problem:** v2.3.1 was live in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an 18% error rate. The test build before it (v2.3.1-rc) had also failed health checks in staging.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production, so I rolled back to it. All three regions now run v2.3.0 and pass health checks, with the error rate down to 0.2%. Change-manager approval wasn't needed because v2.3.0 has been healthy in production before.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) is open and has paged the on-call engineer. It covers the failure, the rollback, the current status, and a note to find out why v2.3.1 failed before deploying it again.", "type": "text"}]}]}